(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// Traceback and frame objects' attributes (Python/traceback.c, Objects/frameobject.c)."] [31 53 "// in bytes (2 × the instruction), the reported one after a reraise N"] [61 2 "// the attributes as the type's getset descriptors too (type(frame).f_locals: inspect.isgetsetdescriptor; dir)"] [81 1 "// FrameLocals is f_locals (frame_locals_get_impl): a module's or class's namespace (its mapping when __prepare__'s or"] [82 1 "// exec's was not a dict), else PEP 667's write-through proxy over the frame's fast locals, cells and free variables."] [90 1 "// frameNamespace is a module's or class's body's namespace (its mapping when not a dict), nil for a function's frame,"] [91 1 "// and nil while an inlined comprehension of the body has its own names bound (PEP 709's hidden locals: CPython's"] [92 1 "// _PyFrame_HasHiddenLocals, the proxy then over them and the extra locals)."] [108 1 "// frameSetAttr is frame's setters (f_trace, f_trace_lines, f_trace_opcodes, f_lineno) and its read-only attributes'"] [109 1 "// refusals, as frameobject.c's getset and member tables answer them; v nil: del."] [144 3 "// frame_lineno_set_impl: a jump is a trace function's, on a line event; pyi runs no trace function"] [145 3 "// (sys.settrace is a no-op), so every write is the one made outside a trace function"] [156 1 "// frameExecuting is f running: on the current thread's chain of frames, or a running generator's."] [171 1 "// frameClear is frame.clear() (frame_clear_impl): an executing or suspended frame refused; a generator's not started"] [172 1 "// closed; else the locals, cells, value stack, extra locals and f_trace dropped (frame_tp_clear), the code, globals,"] [173 1 "// builtins and f_back kept."] [199 1 "// FrameLocalsProxy is frame.f_locals of a function's frame (PEP 667; Objects/frameobject.c's PyFrameLocalsProxy_Type):"] [200 1 "// a mapping over the frame itself, reads and writes going to its fast locals and cells, so a write is seen by the"] [201 1 "// frame's code at its next load (the loop's and the compiled code's loads read f.Fast and f.Cells, never a copy:"] [202 1 "// survey \"Design: 219\"); a name none of the code's goes to the frame's extra locals."] [205 1 "// FrameLocalsProxyType is the proxy's type (\"FrameLocalsProxy\", registered as a Mapping by _collections_abc)."] [210 1 "// frameSlot is one of a code's names in co_localsplusnames' order: the fast locals (a parameter that is a cell read"] [211 1 "// through its cell), then the cells that are no parameter, then the free variables."] [214 18 "// the index in f.Fast or f.Cells, -1 for the other"] [215 18 "// an earlier slot has the name (each)"] [251 1 "// slotValue is s's value in f, nil when unbound."] [280 1 "// slotOf is framelocalsproxy_getkeyindex: the slot of key's name, an exact str by its text, else any key by its hash"] [281 1 "// and ==; read: only a bound one. -1 when none."] [333 1 "// set is framelocalsproxy_setitem (v nil: del): a local's slot written, never removed; else the extra locals."] [365 1 "// each calls fn on the bound names and their values in order, then the extra locals'. A name twice among the slots"] [366 1 "// (an inlined comprehension's own name in a fast slot beside the function's cell of that name, while the comprehension"] [367 1 "// runs: GH-128396's case, one slot in CPython holding the plain value) gives its first bound slot's value."] [393 1 "// dict is the proxy's items as a new dict (PyDict_Update(dict, proxy))."] [405 1 "// merge is framelocalsproxy_merge: other a dict or a proxy, each of its keys set; false for another mapping."] [505 2 "// nb_or: either operand the proxy, the result a dict of the left's items, then the right's"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[69 42] [84 28] [146 23] [161 25] [162 19] [162 29] [181 15] [182 25] [289 24] [299 22] [321 21] [322 26] [372 25] [374 14] [374 38] [382 19] [383 44] [408 39] [410 34] [415 26] [426 24] [439 35] [472 36] [479 31] 